			<div class="content" id="post-content-4833435">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Drama/Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Interviews and incident logs to be included.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> : An MTF officer starts to spot in random situations a former squad companion who died in an earlier Containment operation. Despite Foundation help with amnestics, the visions become more frequent and intense.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Adam and Samuel have been friends since nursery times: they attended the same high school and joined the police academy at the same time. After some time in a police station, they are recruited by the SCP Foundation to join a MTF. Some years later, during a Containment operation, Samuel fails to follow protocol and ends up with Adam dead. The grief and sense of guilt pursuits Samuel to the point that starts to see Adam during his routine more often with time, to the point that jeopardizes other companions during some MTF operations. After a psychological test, he is given an amnestic to forget about his friend and stick to the MTF.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>However, after some time without issues, during an intense MTF operation, Samuel provokes a containment breach as he claims that an unknown individual appeared to him. This appearance will never leave from then on. After providing a description to the psychologist, matching that of Adam, he is given another amnestic. The entity does not disappear though, and it starts to directly intervene in Adam’s actions, deterring him from any basic activity. Foundation demotes him and keeps him a study subject in order to prevent further failed operations, classifying Adam’s apparition as an SCP object. Eventually, Samuel commits suicide. An MTF operative from Samuel’s former MTF squad is recorded in a tapped phone call claiming that he has spotted Samuel in his garden and is afraid of reporting this to the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Adam’s apparition to Samuel is not real. It is driven by strong feelings of guilt, grief and melancholy. The abnormality comes from the exaggerated expression of these feelings, which get so stuck to Samuel and his subconscious that even amnestics cannot fully support Samuel. So to avoid jeopardizing future operations, Foundation classifies it as an anomaly. Samuel’s sorrow becomes a memetic effect.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> There are two main ideas that I wanted to explore. First, how even long-term friendship can deeply mark an individual; and second, the HRM policy of the Foundation regarding its MTF operatives, and the perils of mental health mismanagement.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
